/*
UpsertOrganization Upsert a billing organization (idempotent)

Idempotent upsert of the organization a merchant platform bills for. The org id is
the platform's own tenant key. `billing_currency` participates in the one-way
currency lock — it is applied only on **create**, never rewritten for an existing org.

Send the full billing address before selling a paid plan. Tax is resolved from
`billing_country`, and for a US state or a Canadian province from
`billing_subdivision` too; every invoice prints the street, postal code and city
(`billing_address_line1`, `billing_postal_code`, `billing_city`; no postal code where the
country has none). A paid subscribe or plan change on an organization without them is
refused with `422 billing_address_required`, naming the `missing` fields. Each address
field is optional here and applied only when sent; send `null` to clear one. The address
is copied onto every document at issue, so a later change never alters an invoice already
issued.

One product owns the organization's account (INT-13): the one whose token created it, or
the first one to subscribe it while its owner holds no subscription on it. A
product-bound token writes the account when its product owns it, or nobody owns it and no
other product bills it. Any other product-bound token is still answered `200`, never `404`,
with `account: shared`. That upsert changes nothing the owner set (name, billing email,
address, locale, purchaser type, EAN, order reference) and only fills `billing_country` and
`billing_subdivision` while the organization has no country. When the caller's product
bills the organization, or no other product does (the caller's subscribe would take the
account over), it also fills the name, billing email, address, `purchaser_type`,
`ean_number` and `order_reference` fields that are still empty; upsert again after
subscribing to write them in full. Its answer leaves out the owner's billing email,
address and order reference.

`purchaser_type` states who the customer buys as (a state government, a charity, an
embassy under EU Art. 151, a public body). It asks the place's own rule and never
exempts by itself: most rules relieve only against a verified exemption certificate of a
matching kind. A Danish public body (`public_body` in `DK`) needs a valid `ean_number`
before an invoice can be issued; until then its invoices are held and issued once it is
set.


 @param ctx context.Context - for authentication, logging, cancellation, deadlines, tracing, etc. Passed from http.Request or context.Background().
 @param org The organization id (the merchant platform's own tenant key).
 @return ApiUpsertOrganizationRequest
*/
